-<p>Explicit feature-close driver over the durable coordinator; interrupted runs require an exact lifecycle ID to resume. A lost final process response can be resolved read-only against the closed State, coordinator and audit references without a duplicate close; this never implies release authorization. Also projects the dispatch records into the audit bundle, exports every Critic round from the private journal inside the close commit, states the security scope, stops early on a Critic round that did not pass and routes a declined acceptance back into a correction round (a completed package returns to implementing for a proven correction). Before the acceptance question the one-shot close checks or writes the SBOM from the tracked lockfiles and stops on a stale, invalid, partial or unsupported finding unless a human&#39;s literal override is recorded, names the SBOM record in the audit request, and with the last argument --stage stages exactly the paths of the commit its result asks for without committing.</p>
